         "step": 1,
         "text": "The integrand has the shape of an inverse trigonometric derivative, \\( \\frac{d}{dx} \\arctan\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right) = \\frac{6}{36 + x^{2}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "antiderivative read from a derivative rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "With \\( u = \\frac{x}{6}, \\; dx = 6\\,du \\), the integral becomes \\( \\int \\frac{4}{36\\left(1 + u^{2}\\right)} \\cdot 6\\,du = \\frac{2}{3} \\int \\frac{du}{1 + u^{2}} \\), which is \\( \\frac{2 \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{6} \\right)}}{3} + C \\).",
